  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153259,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> conventional or classic lipoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153260,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153261,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These most commonly occur in the vulva but may occur at any location.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153262,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoma presents as a superficial, solitary, soft, mobile, and painless mass {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153263,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are rare entities in the female genital tract, with an estimated incidence of just 0.03% of all gynaecological tumours {36782265}. Lipomas occur in adults of reproductive age, as well as in children {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153264,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153265,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>An abnormal karyotype is present in the majority of conventional lipomas. The most common alteration involves 12q13-q15, resulting in fusion of <em>HMGA2</em> with a variety of gene partners {9530339}. Other reported chromosomal abnormalities include 6p and 13q rearrangements {9530339}. <em>MDM2</em> amplification is not a feature.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153266,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are lobulated, well circumscribed, and sometimes covered by a thin membrane. The cut surface is homogeneously yellow, with thin fibrous septa dividing the tumour into lobules. Focal haemorrhage can be present {19853747}. Tumours have been reported to exceed 150&nbsp;mm in greatest dimension {24629715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153267,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours consist of a relatively uniform population of mature adipocytes arranged in sheets and/or separated into lobules by thin fibrous septa {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}. Adipocytes and septal stromal cells lack cytological atypia; lipoblasts are not present. Degenerative changes, including myxoid stromal change and fat necrosis, can occur, particularly in larger tumours. Tumours lack MDM2 and CDK4 expression by immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153268,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears are variably cellular, composed of tissue fragments of mature adipocytes. There are uniform adipocytes containing a single large cytoplasmic clear vacuole and small nuclei with inconspicuous nucleoli against a background that is bloody with fat globules and small round open spaces {12920746}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153269,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153270,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 211,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> superficial location; uniformly sized mature adipocytes; lack of atypical stromal cells in fibrous septa.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153271,
        "bookId": 85,
